      "math_academy_id": "q-290907",
      "problem": "Suppose we have a dataset consisting of $5$ datapoints with $3$ features in the form of the $5\\times 3$ matrix\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}5.711 & 3.866 & -3.400 \\\\ 3.580 & -0.216 & -3.789 \\\\ -0.507 & -5.693 & -3.727 \\\\ 1.640 & -0.269 & 0.705 \\\\ -0.225 & -4.111 & -2.130\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe wish to reduce the dimensionality of the dataset while still preserving as much variance as possible.\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning that walks through the process of reducing the dimensionality of the dataset.\n\nWe will use principal component analysis to reduce the dimensionality of the dataset. The first principal component is \n{{field-1}} \nwith the \n{{field-2}} \nvariance.\n\nThe second principal component is the direction in feature space \n{{field-3}} \nto the first\n{{field-4}}.",
